= Expanding Healthcare

@healthcare_menu

- @use_section_1115: Approve medicaid expansions
- @crack_down_on_overpayments: Crackdown on medicare advantage fraud
- @healthcare_legislation: Go to legislative options
- @easy_discard


@use_section_1115
subtitle: Provisions in Medicaid allow us to approve of "experimental" healthcare coverage by other states. This has historically been used to help lower income mothers the most.
choose-if: medicare_for_all = 0
max-visits: 2
unavailable-subtitle: Our previous healthcare reforms makes this irrelevant. 
on-arrival: {!
Q.progressive_dissent -=3
Q.socialist_dissent -=3
Q.healthcare_cost_progress +=3
Q.nat_support.age.mid +=2
Q.nat_support.inc.low +=2
Q.nat_support.inc.high -=1
window.simulate_polling();
!}

Fine. By cutting welfare, we have reduced dissent within the coalition.

@crack_down_on_overpayments
subtitle: +0.40 budget. Insurers are attempting to make seniors look sicker then they actually are to reciece higher government payouts. These practices cost the government money and make healthcare more expensive for everyone
view-if: historical_mode = 0
max-visits: 2
on-arrival: {!
Q.budget +=0.4
Q.socialist_dissent -=3
Q.healthcare_cost_progress +=3
Q.nat_support.age.senior +=3
Q.corporate_backlash +=1
window.simulate_polling();
!}

By transferring campaign funds to our coalition partners, we can make our policies more acceptable to them. Some would call this corruption, but perhaps it is necessary to save democracy.

@healthcare_legislation

- @drug_negotiation: Empower Medicare to negotiate lower drug prices
- @healthcare_menu: Go back to executive action

